obs the lesson this lap surfaced: writing an intermediate held-still log mid-pass is safe only when a LATER round-open intervenes to stash it before the pass's own close reads the tree; a turn that watches one pass through to its own completion, as this one did with Monitor, has no such intervening round-open, so the file stays untracked straight through to the close and the pass reads tree_moved=yes on its own honest output -- named in the next-log entry as guidance for a future lap in the same shape
